Comskip compatibility with FFmpeg 8, applied to upstream commit a140b6ac8bc8f596729e9052819affc779c3b377.

Derived from erikkaashoek/Comskip pull request 187, "Allow build with ffmpeg-8.0"
(https://github.com/erikkaashoek/Comskip/pull/187, head 8725a3c15bc9e0a6e2797e04c1433dd8bd43b5e4).
FFmpeg 8 removes AVCodecContext.ticks_per_frame. The pull request replaces it with
(codec_descriptor->props & AV_CODEC_PROP_FIELDS), which is 16 or 0, not the 2 or 1 it stood for, so this patch
computes 2 for field-coded codecs and 1 otherwise, and keeps the MPEG-1 override. codec_descriptor and
AV_CODEC_PROP_FIELDS exist in FFmpeg 6.1 too, so it builds there as well.

--- a/mpeg2dec.c
+++ b/mpeg2dec.c
@@ -43,6 +43,14 @@
 #include <libavutil/pixdesc.h>
 #include <libavutil/samplefmt.h>
 #include <libswscale/swscale.h>
+
+/* AVCodecContext.ticks_per_frame is gone in FFmpeg 8: 2 for codecs that code fields (MPEG-2, H.264), 1 otherwise. */
+static int codec_ticks_per_frame(const AVCodecContext *ctx)
+{
+    if (ctx->codec_id == AV_CODEC_ID_MPEG1VIDEO)
+        return 1;
+    return ctx->codec_descriptor && (ctx->codec_descriptor->props & AV_CODEC_PROP_FIELDS) ? 2 : 1;
+}
 
 #ifdef HARDWARE_DECODE
 #include <fftools/ffmpeg.h>
